1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,568
Your watchlists decide what the dashboard shows:

2
00:00:02,588 --> 00:00:05,313
the signal tables, the chart, and your scans.

3
00:00:05,363 --> 00:00:06,901
Let's set them up.

4
00:00:07,365 --> 00:00:11,362
First, open Settings in the sidebar and choose the markets you trade:

5
00:00:11,382 --> 00:00:13,254
cryptos, equities, or both.

6
00:00:13,304 --> 00:00:15,546
The other market's sections hide.

7
00:00:15,992 --> 00:00:19,023
Then tick that step on the getting-started checklist.

8
00:00:20,242 --> 00:00:22,953
Now open Watchlists, then Edit Crypto.

9
00:00:23,003 --> 00:00:26,375
Type a name or a ticker, press Enter, and pick the match.

10
00:00:26,425 --> 00:00:27,983
Here, Chainlink.

11
00:00:28,033 --> 00:00:29,853
The first time anyone adds a coin,

12
00:00:29,873 --> 00:00:34,392
its readings are worked out and saved for everyone, so it takes a few seconds.

13
00:00:34,442 --> 00:00:36,385
After that, it's instant.

14
00:00:40,539 --> 00:00:43,079
Shares work the same way, in Edit Stocks.

15
00:00:43,129 --> 00:00:46,266
Type a company or a ticker. Here, AMD.

16
00:00:46,316 --> 00:00:49,347
Again, a new one takes a few seconds the first time.

17
00:00:57,832 --> 00:01:02,484
Both now appear in the signal tables, with their Trend, Stretch and Flow readings.

18
00:01:07,168 --> 00:01:10,561
To take one off, choose it under Remove, in the same place.

19
00:01:11,048 --> 00:01:14,249
Three or more assets ticks the watchlist step by itself.

20
00:01:14,299 --> 00:01:17,693
Your watchlists are saved on your account, on every device.
